== Vocabulary ==
The table below presents a sample of Mohican words, written first in a linguistically oriented transcription, followed by the same words written in a practical system that has been used in the linguistically related dialect of Munsee.<ref>Goddard, Ives, 1982; O'Meara, John, 1996</ref> The linguistic system uses a raised dot (·) to indicate vowel length. Although stress is mostly predictable, the linguistic system uses the acute accent to indicate predictable main stress. As well, predictable voiceless or murmured {{IPA|/ă/}} is indicated with the breve accent (˘). Similarly, the breve accent is used to indicate an ultra-short {{IPA|[ə]}} that typically occurs before a single voiced consonant followed by a vowel.<ref>See Goddard, Ives, 1982, p. 19 for further detail</ref> The practical system indicates vowel length by doubling the vowel letter, and maintains the linɡuistic system's practices for marking stress and voiceless/ultra-short vowels. The practical system uses orthographic {{angbr|sh}} for the phonetic symbol {{IPA|/š/}}, and {{angbr|ch}} for the phonetic symbol {{IPA|/č/}}.<ref>O'Meara, John, 1996</ref>

